{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790963602,"nonce":"a0cW7NuqyliKYJa40Rzo/WjU+LU=","message":"Issue9601 is this: `Std.string(Array\u003cString\u003e)` calls the untyped `haxe_array_to_string`, whose `format_array_slot` (runtime/src/haxe_sys.rs) prints \"\" as an integer and any pointer above USER_HEAP_HI as an integer (Linux CI heap addresses are ~0x5579..). Through Dynamic, `haxe_box_reference_ptr(arr, 7)` uses `array_to_string` (type_system.rs), which assumes DynamicValue elements: \"\" prints null, \"Test\" \u003cunknown type\u003e. The regex results themselves are right. Upstream compiles the test only under `#if (jvm || eval)`; it runs here because rayzor defines `eval`.","files":null}]}